Spec: Fillet Tool

Purpose:
  Round sharp corners on paths by replacing corner nodes with smooth arcs.

Owns:
  ./fillet.ts
  ./fillet.test.ts

Must:
  Configurable radius in mm (via UI panel).
  Click on a corner node applies fillet to that corner.
  Only works on nodes with straight (line) segments on both sides.
  Replaces the corner node with a smooth arc approximation.
  Fillet operation is fully undoable.
  Preview shows expected arc before clicking.

Must not:
  Apply fillet to nodes that are already smooth.
  Apply fillet when radius exceeds available segment length.
  Modify nodes other than the clicked one.

Depends on:
  @BaseTool
  @PathShape
  @FilletCommand
  @SnapManager

Scenario: round fillet with positive radius
  Given a rectangle with 4 corner nodes and fillet radius = 5mm
  When the user clicks the top-left corner
  Then the corner is replaced with a 5mm radius arc (convex)
  And the path now has 5 nodes (3 corners + 2 new smooth nodes for the arc)
  And the arc curves toward the interior of the corner

Scenario: round fillet with negative radius (inward arc)
  Given a rectangle with 4 corner nodes and fillet radius = -5mm
  When the user clicks a corner node
  Then the corner is replaced with a concave arc (curving away from corner)
  And the arc has a radius of curvature matching |5mm|
  And the path has additional nodes (multi-segment for accuracy)

Scenario: bevel fillet
  Given a rectangle and fillet style set to 'bevel' with radius = 5mm
  When the user clicks a corner node
  Then the corner is replaced with a straight chamfer (bevel)
  And the two new nodes have no curves (corner type, cpIn=cpOut=position)
  And the path now has 5 nodes

Scenario: preview on hover (round)
  Given the Fillet tool is active and radius = 5mm
  When the user hovers over a valid corner node
  Then a green arc preview appears on the canvas
  And the cursor indicates a clickable state

Scenario: preview on hover (bevel)
  Given the Fillet tool is active, style = bevel, radius = 5mm
  When the user hovers over a valid corner node
  Then a green straight-line preview appears on the canvas

Scenario: reject fillet on smooth node
  Given a path with a smooth node (has bezier curves)
  When the user clicks that smooth node with the Fillet tool
  Then nothing happens (fillet only works on straight corners)
  And the node count remains unchanged

Scenario: reject fillet when radius exceeds segment length
  Given a small triangle and fillet radius = 50mm (larger than any edge)
  When the user clicks a corner
  Then nothing happens (radius rejected as too large)
  And the node count remains unchanged

Scenario: reject negative radius for bevel style
  Given fillet style = bevel and radius = -5mm
  When the user clicks a corner node
  Then nothing happens (negative not allowed for bevel)

Scenario: undo round fillet
  Given a rectangle has had a fillet applied (5 nodes)
  When the user presses Ctrl+Z
  Then the original 4-node rectangle is restored

Scenario: undo bevel
  Given a rectangle has had a bevel applied (5 nodes)
  When the user presses Ctrl+Z
  Then the original 4-node rectangle is restored

Scenario: fillet radius input accepts negative values
  Given the Fillet tool is active and style is 'round'
  When the user types "-10" in the radius input field
  Then the store's filletRadius is set to -10 * PIXELS_PER_MM
  And the preview uses the negative radius

Scenario: switching to bevel resets negative radius
  Given the fillet radius is -5mm and style is 'round'
  When the user changes style to 'bevel'
  Then the radius resets to 0 (bevel does not support negative)

Tasks:
  [x] Click to apply fillet.
  [x] Configurable radius.
  [x] Preview arc on hover.
  [x] Validation (straight segments required).
  [x] Undoable via command.
